{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4R2YfNAizyCNDCrgaT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`FilePathField` now accepts a callable for `path`, so a migration can store a reference to a function instead of a path that was worked out on the machine where `makemigrations` ran.\n\n**The fix:** a one-line change in `formfield()` (`django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1712`). If `path` is a callable, it's called there to get the directory; otherwise the value is used as before.\n\n**Migrations:** `deconstruct()` already passes `self.path` through untouched, so the migration writer saves the function by import path rather than as a resolved string. I didn't run `makemigrations` to confirm that.\n\n**Docs:** I added a short note and example to `docs/ref/models/fields.txt`. For the issue's model it looks like this:\n\n```python\ndef images_path():\n    return os.path.join(settings.LOCAL_FILE_DIR, 'images')\n\nfile = models.FilePathField(path=images_path)\n```\n\n**Tests:** the existing `model_fields` and `forms_tests.field_tests.test_filepathfield` suites pass (270 run, 48 skipped). No test passes a callable yet, so this case is untested. I couldn't add one because the rules say not to edit test files.\n\nThe function has to be defined at module level so migrations can import it. A lambda won't work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":20189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"output_tokens":415,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb6aa9f0-4cf1-483a-bef4-cc5079ca785b","uuid":"748cc694-a493-4487-969c-1ae20d09c29e","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:19:53.207Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4R2P1EVm2XiRQ